=== Worked example, clocks (4D) ===
Setup: Clocks are local: one step east, a clock reads one step later than a clock one step west of it at the same moment. Premises marked by local clocks give the time as the clocks where the two things are read it; the rest use the station clock.
       Each premise is one step on every dimension it names.
Premises:
  By local clocks, Eve is west, south, below and later relative to Fay.
  Cole is east, south, above and earlier relative to Ash.
  Dell is west, south, below and earlier relative to Ash.
  By local clocks, Eve is west, same latitude, same height and earlier relative to Bell.
  By local clocks, Ash is east, south, above and earlier relative to Bell.
Question: By the station clock, is Fay later or earlier relative to Dell, or at the same time?
Answer:   later   (vector in the asked reading [0,3,1,1])
  lure literal       same time
  lure wrong way     earlier
  lure all marked    same time
  lure other reading later   (= answer)
  derivation:
    Ash - Bell: stated [1,-1,1,-1] (marked) -> world [1,-1,1,-2]
    Cole - Ash: stated [1,-1,1,-1]
    Dell - Ash: stated [-1,-1,-1,-1]
    Eve - Bell: stated [-1,0,0,-1] (marked) -> world [-1,0,0,0]
    Eve - Fay: stated [-1,-1,-1,1] (marked) -> world [-1,-1,-1,2]
  Fay - Dell in world: [0,3,1,1]; depth 4

=== Worked example, drift (4D) ===
Setup: A barge drifts one step east for every step of time. Premises marked aboard measure east and west on the barge; the rest measure from the bank.
       Each premise is one step on every dimension it names.
Premises:
  Aboard, Dell is west, north, below and earlier relative to Cole.
  Dell is west, north, below and earlier relative to Fay.
  Bell is west, south, below and earlier relative to Cole.
  Aboard, Eve is west, south, below and same time relative to Ash.
  From the bank, Bell is same longitude, south, above and later relative to Ash.
Question: Aboard, is Eve east or west relative to Fay, or at the same longitude?
Answer:   east   (vector in the asked reading [1,-1,-3,-2])
  lure literal       west
  lure wrong way     west
  lure all marked    west
  lure other reading west
  derivation:
    Bell - Ash: stated [0,-1,1,1]
    Bell - Cole: stated [-1,-1,-1,-1]
    Dell - Cole: stated [-1,1,-1,-1] (marked) -> world [-2,1,-1,-1]
    Eve - Ash: stated [-1,-1,-1,0] (marked) -> world [-1,-1,-1,0]
    Dell - Fay: stated [-1,1,-1,-1]
  Eve - Fay in world: [-1,-1,-3,-2]; depth 5

